{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","text":"HTTPTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next batch sent only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once the previous one is delivered or dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The method is "},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/context"},{"type":"text","text":", so a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names are the instrument’s: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"type":"text","text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", whatever a configured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field or the instrument wrote.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body"},{"text":" for the batch’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request the transport can never send ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an "},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Retry-After","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the batch, and it isn’t sent again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A batch the endpoint rejects,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose request can’t be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped: logged at error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level and reported on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns without logging or reporting it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which drops its oldest batch when full and reports it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). With a store, a dropped batch’s records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"aren’t lost: once this destination has caught up, the delivery reads them back from the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and hands them to it again, in the same run, so they are sent once the endpoint answers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, the records of a dropped batch are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","symbolKind":"struct","title":"HTTPDestination","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L67"},"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDesti